SLUG: contact.html
TITLE: Contact Akash Movers, Kanpur — request a callback
DESC: Call or WhatsApp +91 98391 00644 to arrange a move in Kanpur. Our office is at 113/186, Swaroop Nagar, Kanpur 208002.
HEADING: Talk to us about your move
LEAD: Leave your name and number and we will call you back. Tell us what is moving and where it is going, and you will get a written, itemised quote with no obligation.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Contact|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="contact-grid">

        <div>
          <h2>How to reach us</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            The quickest route is WhatsApp — you can send photos of the rooms
            and we can scope most moves from those without a visit.
          </p>

          <ul class="contact-list mt-6">
            <li data-contact-phone hidden>
              <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-phone"/></svg>
              <div>
                <span class="label">Phone</span>
                <a data-tel-link><span data-config="contact.phoneDisplay"></span></a>
              </div>
            </li>

            <!-- Any additional numbers from `contact.secondaryContacts`.
                 Rendered by renderSecondaryContacts() in js/main.js, and
                 removed entirely when that list is empty. -->
            <li data-contact-second hidden>
              <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-phone"/></svg>
              <div>
                <span class="label">Also</span>
                <span data-second-contacts></span>
              </div>
            </li>

            <li data-contact-wa hidden>
              <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-whatsapp"/></svg>
              <div>
                <span class="label">WhatsApp</span>
                <a data-wa-link><span data-config="contact.whatsappDisplay">Message us</span></a>
              </div>
            </li>

            <li data-contact-email hidden>
              <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-mail"/></svg>
              <div>
                <span class="label">Email</span>
                <a data-mail-link><span data-config="contact.email"></span></a>
              </div>
            </li>

            <li data-contact-address hidden>
              <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-pin"/></svg>
              <div>
                <span class="label">Office</span>
                <span data-footer-address></span>
              </div>
            </li>

            <li>
              <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg>
              <div>
                <span class="label">Hours</span>
                <span data-opening-hours>Monday to Saturday, 9am – 7pm. Sunday, 10am – 4pm.</span>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>

          <!-- Shown only while no contact details have been configured, so
               the page never looks broken during setup. Removed by main.js
               as soon as a real phone number or email exists. -->
          <div class="demo-banner mt-6" data-contact-unset hidden>
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-alert"/></svg>
            <div>
              <strong>Contact details not configured yet.</strong>
              Add the phone number, WhatsApp number and email in
              <code>js/config.js</code> and they will appear here, in the footer
              and in the structured data automatically.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="btn-row mt-7">
            <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="#callback">Request a callback</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="card">
            <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-receipt"/></svg></span>
            <h3>What to have ready</h3>
            <p>
              You do not need any of this to get started — but having it to hand
              makes the quote accurate the first time, rather than after two
              phone calls.
            </p>
            <ul class="ticks">
              <li>
                <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
                <span>Both addresses, with the floor number and whether there is a working lift</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
                <span>A rough idea of how far the truck can park from the door</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
                <span>Anything oversized or fragile: double-door fridge, piano, glass tabletop, aquarium</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
                <span>Whether you want us to pack everything, or only the kitchen and breakables</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
                <span>Your preferred date, and whether it can move by a day or two</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="card mt-5">
            <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg></span>
            <h3>What happens next</h3>
            <ol class="steps mt-0">
              <li class="step"><div>
                <h4>We reply the same working day</h4>
                <p>Usually within a couple of hours during office hours.</p>
              </div></li>
              <li class="step"><div>
                <h4>We survey, in person or over video</h4>
                <p>Ten minutes on a video call is enough for most flats.</p>
              </div></li>
              <li class="step"><div>
                <h4>You get an itemised written quote</h4>
                <p>Packing, labour, transport and any extras listed separately, so you can see what drives the price.</p>
              </div></li>
              <li class="step"><div>
                <h4>You decide</h4>
                <p>No deposit is taken to hold a quote, and the quote does not expire the same week.</p>
              </div></li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Map. Hidden until real coordinates exist in js/config.js, because an
       approximate pin on a moving company is worse than no pin at all. -->
  <!-- The map is built by renderMap() in js/main.js. It is centred on the
       configured coordinates when they exist, and on the written address when
       they do not — never on an invented approximation. The section stays
       hidden if neither is available. -->
  <section class="section is-tight on-sunk" data-map-section hidden>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Find us</span>
        <h2>Where we are based</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Our office is on Swaroop Nagar. You are welcome to
          come and talk a move through in person before booking anything.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- The board over the door, so a visitor knows what to look for when
           they get there. Not decoration: the GSTIN and both numbers on it
           are the same ones printed on this page, which is the point. -->
      <figure class="board-shot">
        <img src="/assets/images/signboard-640.jpg"
             srcset="/assets/images/signboard-640.jpg 640w,
                     /assets/images/signboard-1000.jpg 1000w"
             sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 30rem, 100vw"
             alt="The Akash Movers signboard, showing the GSTIN, both contact numbers and the address at 113/186, Swaroop Nagar."
             width="1000" height="747" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <figcaption>Look for this board at 113/186, Swaroop Nagar.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="map" data-map>
        <p class="map__empty">Map loads once the office address is configured.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="map__note text-sm mt-4" data-map-note hidden></p>
      <div class="btn-row mt-5">
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" data-map-directions hidden>
          <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-route"/></svg>
          Get directions
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The callback form itself, in the page rather than behind a button.
       This is the contact page: a visitor who reached it has already decided
       to get in touch, and asking them to click once more to see a form is
       a step that only loses people. js/callback-form.js mounts it. -->
  <section class="section on-sunk" id="callback" aria-labelledby="callback-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split is-wide-left">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Request a callback</span>
          <h2 id="callback-title">Ready when you are</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            Your name and number is all we need to start. We will call you back,
            talk through what is moving and where it is going, and arrange a
            survey if you want one.
          </p>
          <div class="btn-row mt-6">
            <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" data-wa-link hidden>
              <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-whatsapp"/></svg>
              Chat on WhatsApp instead
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div data-callback-form>
          <noscript>
            <p class="form-note">
              This form needs JavaScript. Please call or message us instead — the
              number is at the top of this page.
            </p>
          </noscript>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
